/users/lukors/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukors/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukors/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukors/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukors/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukors/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukors/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-06T11:38:13Z","updated_at":"2025-06-06T11:38:13Z","body":"The behavior they see there is more reasonable, because they set the time scale to like 50x normal, which would mean the engine skips physics updates entirely. So it makes some sense that it would be incorrect.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2948979596/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3592402493","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107203#issuecomment-3592402493","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107203","id":3592402493,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7WH7Y9","user":{"login":"Rudolph-B","id":52322745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzIyNzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52322745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B","html_url":"https://github.com/Rudolph-B","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-30T09:45:19Z","updated_at":"2025-11-30T09:45:19Z","body":"I was able to replicate the behavior. This issue is inherited from SceneTreeTimer (#96626) as the timer node was implemented to copy its behavior. A issue already exists for this behavior in SceneTreeTimer (#94355).\n\nAs pointed out in #94355 the behavior is entirely linked to what your rendered frame rate is, which I believe is unwanted behavior if you set your timer to be linked to the physics process frame.\n\n> Godot v4.6.dev4 - Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS 24.04 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 SUPER (nvidia; 570.195.03) - AMD Ryzen 7 3700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 15.52 GiB memory","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3592402493/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]